# Pictures in web pages: `browse` loads a page's <img> pictures (from the
# disk here; from the web the same way), makes them fit the window and
# draws them where the page keeps lines for them. At 800x600 the viewer's
# window is the first extra one: content 640x400 at 38,62, lines of 16
# pixels, the page from its second line; pictures at 8 pixels from the left.
@ai
$ ai control on
$ display mode 800x600
~ ^mode: 800x600
$ mkdir /site
$ screenshot /site/shot.png
~ ^saved the screen
$ echo "<title>Pictures</title><h1>Pictures</h1><p>above<img src=shot.png alt=desk><img src=missing.png alt=gone><p>below" > /site/p.html
$ browse /site/p.html
/site/p.html in a new window: Tab picks a link, Enter follows it, q leaves
$ sleep 2
# Inside the picture (the screen's light blue desktop, scaled down to
# 427x320 from x=46) and to its right (the page's black background); the
# picture that is not there shows its alt text.
@screenshot 800x600 pixels 60,200=a8d0f0 600,200=000000
# Further down: the alt text of the picture that is not there, and the text after.
@ctl keys {machine} "{pagedown}"
@ctl text {machine}
~ ^\[gone\]$
~ ^below$
@ctl keys {machine} "q"
